\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Sometimes  a light suprises
\par The Christian while he sings;
\par It is the Lord who rises
\par With healing in His wings:
\par When comforts are declining,
\par He gran's the soul again
\par A season of clear shining,
\par To cheer it after rain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In holy contemplation,
\par We sweetly then pursue
\par The theme of God's salvation,
\par And find it ever new.
\par Set free from present sorrow,
\par We cheerfully can say,
\par E'en let the unknown to-morrow
\par Bring with it what it may:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. It can bring with it nothing
\par But He will bear us through;
\par Who gives the lilies clothing
\par Will clothe His people too:
\par Beneath the spreading heavens
\par No creature but is fed;
\par And He who feeds the ravens 
\par Will give His children bread.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thouh vine nor fig-tree neither
\par Their wonted fruit should bear,
\par Though all the field should wither,
\par Nor flocks nor herds be there,
\par Yet, God the same abiding,
\par His praise shall tune my voice;
\par For, while in Him confiding,
\par I cannot but rejoice.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

